{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1476592-alternate-leveling-system","id":1476592,"title":"Alternate leveling system","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-17T10:46:36-07:00","id":1476592,"title":"Alternate leveling system","content":"The xp system is a &quot;out universe&quot; way to get your character stronger and better in the way that according to how the player play he will receive a certain amount of xp in the end of the session.<br /> The problem is what if the character has past few weeks to train himself (to fight, run study the same subject or anything)?<br /> I mean if in one session the characters made a long trip or long training and took days, weeks, or month the amount of xp they receive will be max 5 at the end of the session<br /> That amount is the same if in one session just few hours or one day has past<br /> <br /> If we were to houserule something to explain in game the evolution of the character, what would it be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T11:13:31-07:00","id":1476593,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how much house-ruling is necessary.<br /> <br /> 1) Learning isn't something that happens on a set schedule. Necessity (balanced by stress for long term retention) tends to help boost initial learning processes. The more &quot;active&quot; a character is, the more they learn, because they more they're exposed to new situations to learn from.<br /> <br /> 2) The game already has a cap of 1 dot per trait to raise. This means even in relatively fast paced games, characters are going to grow laterally rather than vertically.<br /> <br /> It seems better to think about important some of the Dark Ages &quot;maturation&quot; systems for XP to spend on prolonged down times so characters grow in games that have longer time frames.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T12:10:59-07:00","id":1476595,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the system to learn rites in wta and vtm and was wondering: you get better by training hard and studying a lot so why not use that kind of system to improve your character's skills?<br /> <br /> You keep training/learning everyday for as many week than the next dot, roll the appropriate pool, get as many success than the level you trying to get and raise the difficulty by 1 each new level<br /> If you try to get your first dot at science you study for one entire weeks, roll Intelligence at diff 6 and must get 1 success. If successful you get you first dot. Same for the second dot but you add Science to your roll, raise the diff by one, must get 2 success and study for 2 entire weeks.<br /> <br /> As i don't have the Dark Age i don't know the others evolution system","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-17T19:03:23-07:00","id":1476623,"title":"","content":"The problem with rolling for advancement, is that it overly incentivizes certain traits. Making a Garou with low Intelligence is a giant pain in the ass because learning rites gets impossible.<br /> <br /> If you take that out to a broader scale, you just end up with highly uneven PCs were some have advanced large amounts, and others are struggling to improve at all.<br /> <br /> There are some advancement systems that make this work, but they're a lot of bookkeeping, as they tend to do things like &quot;You have to critical A times, normal succeed B times, fail C times, and botch D times,&quot; to increase a trait based on your current rating. This tends to aggregate into even PCs over time, but it also makes it harder to increase traits you don't roll.<br /> <br /> ----------<br /> <br /> Maturation is basically just a second pool of XP with different numbers to emphasize what's easy to build up over long periods of time of low activity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T04:02:55-07:00","id":1476642,"title":"","content":"Then we could fix the amount of point a pc can add per Scenario: at the end of the scenario you gor 1 point you can add in your Attributes and 3 in you add in your abilities, but only 1 per abilities<br /> If your character has been using Brawl, Law and medicine enough during the scenario he can add 1 point in each but cannot add 2 or all 3 in the same. <br /> That slow the evolution of the character and the player has to choose in what kind of thing his character is getting better (this system is very far from perfect but i think it is just what it take to mix in and out game mechanics<br /> <br /> In WTA instead of spending xp to buy gift, the spirit ask to success a test to proove he deserve the gift, and in VTM at the end of the scenario the Obtain 1 or 2 point to add in his Disciplines, the more he has the slowest they're evolving","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 03-18-2022, 07:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T10:09:19-07:00","id":1476667,"title":"","content":"Along the same lines as what Heavy Arms is saying, there's also the &quot;Instruction&quot; skill (which can function a handful of different ways depending on which game line and edition you're using,) and in Mage specifically there's the Seasonal studies/experience system (which is explained in the revised era book <i>Guide to the Traditions</i>,) through which can be used to gain experience towards just about anything (including spheres), <i>except</i> Attributes, and (arguably) Arete.<br /> <br /> That said, my group house ruled Instruction so that it can be used to teach greater numbers of people (every RAW version of the skill only permits a single person to benefit) at higher skill levels, and given more time, such that the higher the Instructor's skill, the more people can benefit from their instruction, but the longer any one given 'instruction interval' can take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T11:24:06-07:00","id":1476672,"title":"","content":"I don't have Mage either, but Instruction is an idea if i can find more detailed informations about it.<br /> <br /> But hypothetically if you were to suppress completely the experience system to replace it by a narrative one, the pc declare his character is studying, training, working on one abilitie to improve it, or making some exercises to improve it's attributes, how would it be handled mechanicaly?<br /> <br /> The logic response (for abilities at least) would be to spend certain amount of hours working on it to actively improve them.<br /> The first dozen of hours are used to introduce the character to that skill, so after a time between 10 and 20 hours of hard work he gain his first dot. Next to obtain the second he must work, study, train or anything appropriate for the ability he's working on for at leat 20/30 hours more.<br /> <br /> The higher is the dot he's getting to, the more he must train","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T12:36:21-07:00","id":1476680,"title":"","content":"If you want a more narrative advancement system, you can't really tie it to non-narrative things like units of time.<br /> <br /> You might want to check out the Milestone advancement system from Exalted: Essence. The basics:<br /> <br /> 1) Every increase costs one Milestone regardless of increasing your rating in an Attribute or Ability, or buying a new power.<br /> 2) Each Milestone type says what it can be used to raise (there are four types in Essence: minor, major, personal, and exalted).<br /> 3) Having multiple Milestone types allows you to control the frequency of increases and what narrative events trigger them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T13:35:40-07:00","id":1476682,"title":"","content":"I didn't know this one, pretty interesting but from what i found, it seems to give the st a greater control on the pace leveling of the pc.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, instead of rewarding player act in accordance with their character at the end of the session, why not distribute xp directly during the game according to the exploits and actions of the character?<br /> It would work pretty like renown in werewolf the apocalypse, the character gain 1 xp each time he do something truly useful or impressive<br /> It would reward player according to what they're doing in the game instead of how they play with their character, the more they do the more they gain and if they achieve great actions theyre rewarded a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 03-18-2022, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T13:59:48-07:00","id":1476685,"title":"","content":"So.... you want something more like the Beats system from CofD?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T16:57:20-07:00","id":1476696,"title":"","content":"I don't know this one, wta and vtm are my 2 only rpg \ud83d\ude05","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-18T17:49:48-07:00","id":1476698,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...e-Rules-Update</a> It's a bit hard to understand without knowing the new World of Darkness now the Chronicles of Darkness (hence CofD) but it describes how the Beats system works to general XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}